{
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Verb phrases for the stages of an action",
      "body": "Spanish uses a conjugated verb + (preposition) + infinitive or gerund to describe **when** an action starts, stops, repeats or continues. Only the first verb is conjugated.",
      "table": {
        "head": [
          "Phrase",
          "Meaning",
          "Example"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "*empezar a* + inf.",
            "to start doing",
            "*Empecé a estudiar español en enero.*"
          ],
          [
            "*ponerse a* + inf.",
            "to start (suddenly)",
            "*Se puso a llorar.*"
          ],
          [
            "*acabar de* + inf.",
            "to have just done",
            "*Acabo de llegar.*"
          ],
          [
            "*terminar de* + inf.",
            "to finish doing",
            "*Terminé de trabajar a las seis.*"
          ],
          [
            "*dejar de* + inf.",
            "to stop / quit doing",
            "*Dejé de fumar.*"
          ],
          [
            "*volver a* + inf.",
            "to do again",
            "*Volví a llamar.*"
          ],
          [
            "*seguir* + gerund",
            "to keep / still be doing",
            "*Sigue lloviendo.*"
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "heading": "Acabar de: just",
      "body": "In the present, *acabar de* means \"have just\": *Acabo de comer* (I've just eaten). *¿Acabas de llegar?* In the imperfect, \"had just\": *Acababa de salir cuando me llamaste* (I had just left when you called me)."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Volver a: again",
      "body": "*Volver a* + infinitive is the most natural way to say \"again\": *Volví a ver la película* (I watched the movie again). *No lo vuelvo a hacer* (I won't do it again). You can also say *otra vez* or *de nuevo*: *Lo hice otra vez.*"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Seguir + gerund: still",
      "body": "*Seguir* (e → i) + gerund means to keep doing, or to still be doing: *Sigo estudiando* (I'm still studying). *¿Sigues viviendo en Bogotá?* (Do you still live in Bogotá?) *Siguieron trabajando.*"
    }
  ],
